.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt PISCSI-WEB 1
.Os PiSCSI
.Sh NAME
.Nm piscsi-web
.Nd web control interface for PiSCSI
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl password Ar TOKEN
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
provides the browser-based control interface for a PiSCSI daemon.
It connects to the daemon to display and manage SCSI devices, images,
configuration files, logs, and system services.
.Pp
The packaged service reads its configuration from
.Pa /etc/piscsi-web/piscsi-web.env
and listens on all interfaces at port 8080 by default.
Run the service through
.Xr systemctl 1
on a packaged installation.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl password Ar TOKEN
Use
.Ar TOKEN
to authenticate with the PiSCSI daemon.
This overrides
.Ev PISCSI_TOKEN
for this invocation.
.It Fl v
Print PiSCSI version and copyright information, then exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width SESSION_KEY_FILE
.It Ev SERVER_HOST
Address on which to listen.
The default is
.Dq 0.0.0.0 .
.It Ev SERVER_PORT
TCP port on which to listen.
The default is 8080.
.It Ev PISCSI_HOST
Hostname or IP address of the PiSCSI daemon.
The default is
.Dq localhost .
.It Ev PISCSI_PORT
TCP port of the PiSCSI daemon.
The default is 6868.
.It Ev PISCSI_TOKEN
Authentication token for the PiSCSI daemon.
.It Ev BASE_DIR
Absolute directory that contains disk images.
The default is
.Pa /var/lib/piscsi/images .
.It Ev SHARED_DIR
Absolute directory for shared files.
The default is
.Pa /var/lib/piscsi/shared .
.It Ev CONFIG_DIR
Absolute directory for PiSCSI configuration files.
The default is
.Pa /var/lib/piscsi/config .
.It Ev DRIVER_DIR
Optional absolute directory containing Macintosh hard-disk driver images.
The default is
.Pa /var/lib/piscsi/data/mac-hard-disk-drivers .
.It Ev DRIVE_PROPERTIES_FILE
Drive-properties JSON file.
Packaged installations use
.Pa /etc/piscsi-web/drive_properties.json .
.It Ev MAX_FILE_SIZE
Largest accepted upload in bytes.
The default is 4294967296 (4 GiB).
.It Ev SESSION_KEY_FILE
Absolute path to a base64-encoded master-key file used to protect browser
sessions.
The default is
.Pa /etc/piscsi-web/session.key .
.It Ev SESSION_KEY
Base64-encoded session master key for development only.
It is used only when
.Ev SESSION_KEY_FILE
is not set.
.It Ev SESSION_MAX_AGE
Browser session lifetime in seconds.
The default is 86400.
.It Ev TEMPLATES_DIR
Optional directory containing HTML templates for development.
.It Ev STATIC_DIR
Optional directory containing static assets for development.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the packaged service and inspect its status:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo systemctl enable --now piscsi-web
systemctl status piscsi-web
.Ed
.Pp
Run the application directly against a daemon on another host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PISCSI_HOST=piscsi.local PISCSI_TOKEN=secret piscsi-web
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/piscsi-web/piscsi-web.env
.It Pa /etc/piscsi-web/piscsi-web.env
Packaged service environment file.
.It Pa /etc/piscsi-web/session.key
Packaged session master-key file.
.It Pa /etc/piscsi-web/drive_properties.json
Drive-properties database.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
The web interface can modify PiSCSI devices and files.
Protect access to its listening address, keep the daemon token and session key
secret, and do not make the service publicly reachable without an appropriate
network access control.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr piscsi 1 ,
.Xr scsictl 1
.Pp
Full documentation is available at: <https://www.piscsi.com>
